  "description": "PITJUZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H254 Gd6 Ni6 O56 P6,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.158-3.909 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.73-120.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni6Gd6(μ3-OH)2(OAc)2(O3POct)6(O2CtBu)16]·2MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
